    "content": "Sean Miller is a highly successful college basketball coach, named the 27th head coach at The University of Texas in March 2025. Known for his 12-year tenure at Arizona (2009–2021) and two stints at Xavier, Miller has a career spanning over 20 seasons, featuring multiple Elite Eight appearances and a .700+ winning percentage. He is recognized for rebuilding Arizona and bringing extensive NCAA Tournament experience to Texas. Current Role and Background Current Team: Head Coach at The University of Texas (hired March 2025). Previous Head Coach Roles: Arizona Wildcats (2009–2021) and Xavier Musketeers (2004–2009, 2022–2025). Career Highlights: Over 480 wins, eight regular-season conference titles, four conference tournament championships, and 13+ NCAA Tournament appearances. Achievements: Three-time Pac-10/12 Coach of the Year (2011, 2014, 2017). Coaching Style and Experience \"March\" Success: Frequently reaches the second weekend of the NCAA Tournament, including three Elite Eight runs with Arizona. Player Development: Known for developing NBA talent, including Lauri Markkanen at Arizona. 2021 NCAA Investigation: His tenure at Arizona ended following NCAA charges involving a 2017 investigation. Return to Excellence: Successfully returned to elite coaching status in his second stint at Xavier, leading them to the 2023 Sweet 16. Miller, born in 1968, attended the University of Pittsburgh where he was a standout point guard before beginning his coaching career.",
